Low water walk, 14 November

The harbour office will lead a low water walk across the Sand Spit
on Saturday 14 November, 10:30 to 12:00.

Low water is at 10:52, 0.7 m. The bar is walkable from about 10:10
and covered again by 12:30, so we start on time.

Please bring:
  - boots or old shoes
  - a torch for the Lock Gate culvert
  - warm layers; the spit is exposed

The full tide table for November is attached (tide-table-november.csv),
along with a picture of the harbour mouth and a calendar entry.

Current notices: https://harbour.example/notices
Tide times: https://harbour.example/tides

Harbour Office
office@harbour.example

You are receiving this because lab@reader.example is on the notices list.
